/*
 * lib/website/SLWebsiteGenerator.sleela
 * SLeeLa Standard Library Definition.
 * Definition: Defines the SLeeLa standard-library type SLWebsiteGenerator used within the website library family.
 */
#sleela 1.3
// Unified SLeeLa standard-library front-end object.
// Family: website. The library facade that names the one-call entry point a
// front end (CLI or the JavaFX Website Studio) uses to compose a design + an
// ordered list of signs into a finished, self-contained site.
//
// This file is part of the package "discovery surface": the SLeeLa compiler's
// `run` compiles a single self-contained file, so the executable, all-classes-
// in-one-file build of the generator lives in `lib/website/website.sleela`
// (which inlines SLWebsiteDesign, SLWebsiteSign, SLWebsiteEmitter, and this
// generator with a `main`). This definition documents the facade's shape and
// the preset dial a caller chooses; SLeeLa decides the output. No new VM
// opcode is required -- the generator is String concatenation plus arithmetic.
class SLWebsiteGenerator {
  String presetName;    // "neon" | "aurora" | "brutalist" | "editorial"
  int signCount;        // number of signs composed into the current site

  void choose(String preset) { presetName = preset; }
  void addedSign() { signCount = signCount + 1; }
  int signs() { return signCount; }
  String preset() { return presetName; }
}
